{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":359,"code_snippet":"is_operator_call(){ [[ \"$(o recorded-by)\" == \"$OPERATOR_CMD\" ]]; }","finding":"Operator-only transitions (confirm, reject/supersede of decided rows, context --clear) are gated on a caller-supplied flag; context --clear with the same flag removes the only live signal that would refuse a confirm.","reasoning_trace":"Read is_operator_call (:359) and every caller (:508, :574, :600, :606, :716); checked head settings.json for deny rules (none name dec-write-lib.sh); reproduced on a head-tree copy: new --status proposed, context --set-unattended, confirm refused, context --clear --recorded-by decisions-command rc=0, confirm rc=0, row decided_by operator. Base fence block-destructive-bash.sh:1464-1475 trusts such rows to unlock a spike-branch force-delete.","critique":"disable-model-invocation hides the slash command from the Skill tool only; the Bash tool reaches the script directly and the prose-scanning bats tests are not a runtime control.","remediation":"One-shot nonce minted by the /decisions session and consumed by the operator ops, or a PreToolUse Bash deny on dec-write-lib.sh confirm|context --clear; make context --clear session-bound; reword decisions.md:24-28.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/290.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/863.html","https://owasp.org/Top10/A01_2021-Broken_Access_Control/","DISS-001","DISS-C-001"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":313,"code_snippet":"if is_unattended; then [[ -z \"$ref\" ]] || warn \"unattended context: --answer-ref ignored ...\"; return 0; fi","finding":"An operator confirm under a PRD **Status:** autonomous|unattended signal discards the operator's cli: ref and records decided_by: agent while the row still becomes decided.","reasoning_trace":"op_confirm refuses only on live_run_signal (:509) but derive_attribution short-circuits on is_unattended (:313), which includes the prd signal (:177-180); :538 then sets decided_by to proposed_by. Reproduced with repro-attr.sh: rc=0, WARN printed, list shows agent | decided.","critique":"The same predicate kills operator reject of decided rows (:575) and downgrades operator supersede (:600, :606).","remediation":"Skip the unattended short-circuit when is_operator_call && ! live_run_signal; assert decided_by in tests/unit/dec-write-lib.bats:362-365.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/840.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/778.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"state_machine","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":580,"code_snippet":"r=\"$(printf '%s' \"$r\" | jq -c ... '.status = \"rejected\" ...')\"; begin_tmp; replace_row \"$r\"; verify_and_swap \"$old\" 0 '[$i]'","finding":"op_reject rewrites only the rejected row; the superseded row's supersede_proposed_by keeps pointing at the rejected id, the guard at :600-602 refuses every later agent supersede, the validator (:653-654) accepts the state and the append-only rule (:681-682) forbids nulling the field.","reasoning_trace":"Reproduced: confirm DEC-0001, agent supersede -> DEC-0002, reject DEC-0002 rc=0, DEC-0001.supersede_proposed_by still DEC-0002, agent supersede DEC-0001 rc=1, validate-artifact --type decisions rc=0.","critique":"op_reject and op_supersede each know half of the invariant.","remediation":"Null the old row's pointer in the same write, include it in touched, allow that transition in the validator when the named row is rejected; add a reject-then-supersede test.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/840.html"]}
{"id":"DEVO-001","category":"devops","criterion":"deployment_safety","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":271,"code_snippet":"[[ -f \"$TARGET\" ]] || die \"ledger not found: ${TARGET} (restore the tracked grimoires/loa/decisions.yaml)\"","finding":"The tracked ledger grimoires/loa/decisions.yaml is not in the 39-file change and the writer bootstraps only pending files (:262-270); every live write on a fresh checkout exits 1 and three suites error in setup.","reasoning_trace":"Diff file list has no decisions.yaml; .gitignore negation, validate-gitignore-state tracked set, decisions.md:30-32 and the bats setup() all assume it exists. Suites were green here only with a seeded ledger in the scratch tree.","critique":"Skill prose added by the PR tells unattended runs to call dec-write-lib.sh new, which cannot succeed.","remediation":"Commit the seeded ledger or bootstrap the live file in resolve_target write.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh","line":642,"code_snippet":"rows=\"$(printf '%s' \"$pend\" | jq -c --argjson m \"$map\" '... .decisions[] | walk(if type == \"string\" then rw else . end)')\"","finding":"import appends pending rows verbatim; a pending row carrying status decided, decided_by operator and a well-formed operator: transition lands decided without confirm.","reasoning_trace":"Reproduced: hand-written decisions-pending.yaml with one decided row; import rc=0; DEC-0004 decided/operator. Validator --base-file rule flags operator attribution only under a live unattended signal (:683,:686).","critique":"import is the documented trust boundary between agent-written pending files and the operator-owned ledger; it does not re-derive state.","remediation":"Require status open|proposed, null decided_by/supersedes/supersede_proposed_by and no decided/superseded/rejected transitions on import; add a bats case.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/284.html","DISS-C-002"]}
